Input: {"question": "Who is the main character in the film Jadoo?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 0, "end": 6, "text": "woman."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 7, "end": 71, "text": "Pritam lets her escape, but gets into trouble with his superior."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 72, "end": 125, "text": "Sundari steps forward and asks Pritam to be forgiven."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 126, "end": 202, "text": "Pritam soon finds out that Sundari is in fact a member of a gang of thieves."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 203, "end": 279, "text": "Their leader Rahu who is in jail at present, considers Sundari his property."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 280, "end": 378, "text": "Pritam gets involved in the shady dealings along with Sundari and he is soon hunted by the police."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 379, "end": 462, "text": "The film ends with Pritam shooting Sundari, and getting shot by the police himself."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 463, "end": 535, "text": "The music was composed by Naushad and the lyricist was Shakeel Badayuni."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d00", "start": 536, "end": 565, "text": "Church music was used for the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d01", "start": 0, "end": 8, "text": "Pritam ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d01", "start": 9, "end": 133, "text": "The plot of the film was inspired from The Loves of Carmen ( 1948 ) , directed by Charles Vidor and starring Rita Hayworth ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d01", "start": 134, "end": 229, "text": "[ 5 ] Plot Sundari , a hot-tempered young woman makes her living as a stage dancer and singer ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d01", "start": 230, "end": 284, "text": "She appears to lead a trouble-free , fun amoral life ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d01", "start": 285, "end": 319, "text": "Pritam ( Suresh ) is a constable ."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d01", "start": 320, "end": 359, "text": "When the two meet , they fall in love ."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d01", "start": 360, "end": 422, "text": "Sundari is arrested for a brawl , where she attacked a woman ."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d01", "start": 423, "end": 478, "text": "Pritam lets her escape , but gets into trouble with his"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d02", "start": 0, "end": 4, "text": "Raj."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d02", "start": 5, "end": 125, "text": "The plot of the film was inspired from The Loves of Carmen (1948), directed by Charles Vidor and starring Rita Hayworth."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d02", "start": 126, "end": 217, "text": "[5] Plot Sundari, a hot-tempered young woman makes her living as a stage dancer and singer."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d02", "start": 218, "end": 270, "text": "She appears to lead a trouble-free, fun amoral life."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d02", "start": 271, "end": 299, "text": "Raj (Suresh) is a constable."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d02", "start": 300, "end": 337, "text": "When the two meet, they fall in love."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d02", "start": 338, "end": 398, "text": "Sundari is arrested for a brawl, where she attacked a woman."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d02", "start": 399, "end": 468, "text": "Raj lets her escape, but gets into trouble with his superiors for it."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "who vows revenge on Priyanka."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 30, "end": 103, "text": "He pretends to accept the marriage and marries Aarthi at the last minute."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 104, "end": 192, "text": "Raghu comes to know that Priyanka even murdered her brother in order to live with Raghu."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 193, "end": 290, "text": "The film ends with Priyanka killing herself and Raghu burying Aarthi's chain at Priyanka's grave."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 291, "end": 312, "text": "After working with A."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 313, "end": 315, "text": "R."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 316, "end": 447, "text": "Rahman in his previous project \"Enakku 20 Unakku 18\", Jyothi Krishna decided to work together with Yuvan Shankar Raja in this film."}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 448, "end": 536, "text": "The soundtrack, released on 9 June 2006, consists of 8 tracks with lyrics written by Pa."}, "D4S9": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d03", "start": 537, "end": 593, "text": "Vijay, whilst director Perarasu and Kabilan wrote lyrics"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d04", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "blackmailed by a boy who takes her vulgar photos and he saves her from it ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d04", "start": 76, "end": 141, "text": "Priyanka decides to separate them , and creates photos with him ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d04", "start": 142, "end": 300, "text": "Priyanka finally realises Raghu 's love towards Aarthi , and she tries everything possible to separate them but Pughazhenthy wants Raghu to marry his sister ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d04", "start": 301, "end": 438, "text": "He angers Aarthi by kidnapping and electrifying her , yet she turns normal on seeing Raghu , but worsens when she sees him getting shot ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d04", "start": 439, "end": 525, "text": "In the end , Aarthi goes mental , which enrages Raghu , who vows revenge on Priyanka ."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d04", "start": 526, "end": 537, "text": "He pretends"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d05", "start": 0, "end": 16, "text": "to reunite them."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d05", "start": 17, "end": 91, "text": "She is planning her marriage and is determined that they will both attend."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d05", "start": 92, "end": 164, "text": "Can the men bury the hatchet without actually burying the kitchen knife?"}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d05", "start": 165, "end": 290, "text": "Shalini returns home to Leicester for the Hindu festival of Holi to tell her father and her uncle that she’s getting married."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d05", "start": 291, "end": 571, "text": "But it takes a challenge from a sharp ambitious new restaurant owner who tries to put them out of business and a threat from Shalini that she will not have a traditional Indian wedding before the brothers finally start to unravel the secret behind the quarrel which has lasted two"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d06", "start": 0, "end": 52, "text": ", both wonderful chefs , fall out catastrophically ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d06", "start": 53, "end": 193, "text": "At the climax of their dispute they rip the family recipe book in half – one brother gets the starters and the other gets the main courses ."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d06", "start": 194, "end": 329, "text": "[ 2 ] They set up rival restaurants , on opposite sides of the same road , and spend the next twenty years trying to outdo each other ."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d06", "start": 330, "end": 452, "text": "Neither brother will admit it but they both know they are not entirely successful without the ‘ other half ’ of the menu ."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d06", "start": 453, "end": 503, "text": "It takes Raja 's daughter , Shalini , a successful"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d07", "start": 0, "end": 27, "text": "Gaya is not an Indian E.T ."}, "D8S2": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d07", "start": 28, "end": 34, "text": "' `` ."}, "D8S3": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d07", "start": 35, "end": 47, "text": "Rediff.com ."}, "D8S4": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d07", "start": 48, "end": 93, "text": "Archived from the original on 9 August 2003 ."}, "D8S5": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0399-6cf2a111983b:d07", "start": 94, "end":